  "project_description": "The Views Link Area module provides a \"link\" plugin for Views. It allows customized links to be placed in the header, footer, or empty text of any view. \n\n The obvious use case is to create a list of all nodes of type \"foo\" and then add a header link to the node/add/foo page. By making it a real link rather than just a blob of HTML in a header text area, it gets all the special handling and clean URL friendliness and base-path portability that any Drupal link gets.\n\n Alternative modules \n \n https://www.drupal.org/project/views_add_button \n https://www.drupal.org/project/add_content_by_bundle",
